  <h2>Article Content</h2>
  <div class="article-content">
    <h1>Living Chola Temples: Brihadisvara Architectural Marvels</h1><p>Built by Raja Raja Chola I between 1003 and 1010 CE, the Brihadisvara Temple at Thanjavur represents the zenith of Dravidian temple architecture.</p><h2>The Granite Marvel</h2><p>The entire superstructure rises over 66 meters, topped by an 80-tonne monolithic cupola that was raised via a six-kilometer inclined earth ramp.</p>
  </div>

